---
import BlogLayout from '../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro';

const title = "How to Download Videos on iPhone (Without iTunes)";
const description = "Downloading videos directly to an iPhone used to be incredibly difficult. Thanks to modern iOS updates, it's now easier than ever. Here is how to do it.";
const canonicalUrl = "/blog/how-to-download-videos-on-iphone/";
const datePublished = "2026-07-28";
const breadcrumbName = "Download Videos on iPhone";
---

<BlogLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
  datePublished={datePublished}
  breadcrumbName={breadcrumbName}
>
  <h2>The Old Way vs The New Way</h2>
  <p>
    Years ago, Apple's iOS ecosystem was tightly locked down. To get a downloaded video onto your iPhone, you had to download it on a PC, plug your phone into a cable, and sync it through iTunes. It was a miserable experience.
  </p>
  <p>
    Thankfully, starting with iOS 13, Apple introduced a native Download Manager into Safari and the official Files app. You can now download MP4s directly from the web straight to your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Step-by-Step Guide for iPhone</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Copy the Link:</strong> Open the YouTube, Instagram, or TikTok app. Find the video you want to save, tap the "Share" arrow, and tap "Copy Link".
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Open Safari:</strong> Open the native Safari browser and navigate to <a href="/">mp4yt.com</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Extract the Video:</strong> Paste the copied link into the search bar and tap "Extract".
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tap Download:</strong> Select your preferred resolution (e.g., 1080p) and tap the Download button. 
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Confirm in Safari:</strong> A small popup will appear asking, "Do you want to download this file?". Tap <strong>Download</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Where Did the Video Go?</h2>
  <p>
    Once you tap download, you will see a small blue arrow animate in the Safari address bar (usually at the bottom of the screen). Tap this arrow to see your download progress.
  </p>
  <p>
    By default, the MP4 file is saved to the <strong>Files app</strong> in the "Downloads" folder. 
  </p>

  <h2>How to Move it to your Camera Roll (Photos App)</h2>
  <p>
    If you want the video to show up alongside your personal photos so you can share it on Instagram or iMessage:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the <strong>Files</strong> app on your iPhone.</li>
    <li>Navigate to the "Downloads" folder and tap on the video you just downloaded.</li>
    <li>Tap the <strong>Share</strong> icon (the square with an arrow pointing up) in the bottom left corner.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Save Video</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    That's it! The video is now permanently saved in your Camera Roll.
  </p>
</BlogLayout>
